# Arguments passed to the tierd daemon (word-split by systemd).
#
# The node joins through the seeds compiled into the binary, so no seed argument
# is required; membership is then learned via gossip.
#
# Default (join via the built-in seeds):
TIER_ARGS=run 7777
#
# An explicit seed can be added and is dialed in addition (IPv4/IPv6 literal,
# port as a separate token):
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 203.0.113.10 7777
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 2001:db8::10 7777
#
# The daemon binds the IPv6 wildcard (dual-stack), so it listens on both IPv6
# and IPv4 at the given port.
#
# TIER_NETWORK selects the network (cluster) this node joins; unset means
# mainnet (the production network). Nodes on different networks cannot even
# complete a handshake, so this both picks the preconfigured seeds and isolates
# the node from other clusters. Name: [a-z0-9-], 1-32 chars. Leave unset in
# production.
#   TIER_NETWORK=testnet
#
# TIER_SEEDS fully REPLACES the built-in seeds (private networks, local testing).
# When set and non-empty the node dials only these addresses and never the
# production seeds; leave it unset in production. Comma/space separated,
# "ip:port" with IPv6 bracketed:
#   TIER_SEEDS=[fd00::2]:7777 10.0.0.2:7777
#
# TIER_VERSION_RANGE overrides this network's software-version policy: the
# window of versions this node will participate with. "min,max" with min
# INCLUSIVE and max EXCLUSIVE, so "1.4.0,1.5.0" accepts every 1.4.x and rejects
# 1.5.0. Either side may be empty for an open bound ("1.4.0," >= 1.4.0;
# ",2.0.0" < 2.0.0). A node outside the window refuses to start; a gossiped peer
# outside it is not admitted. This is cluster governance, not security (versions
# are self-reported) and is never sent on the wire. Leave unset to use the baked
# per-network default (currently unconstrained).
#   TIER_VERSION_RANGE=1.4.0,1.5.0
